// What a decorated window's title bar is.
//
// `Standard` is the platform's own bar: the title drawn by the window manager,
// the application's content starting underneath it.
//
// `Unified` is the bar a toolkit draws its own chrome into, the way a macOS
// window with a unified toolbar is built. The content runs the full height of
// the window and under the bar; the bar itself draws nothing — no title, no
// background — and the platform's window controls stay where they belong, sized
// and placed for a toolbar-height band. What goes in that band is the
// application's to draw. A backend whose windows have no such bar treats it as
// `Standard`.
enum WindowTitlebar {
    Standard
    Unified
}
